## Builder Manager — Decomposition

Decompose the build setup phase into worker subtasks.

### Phase Deliverables
- `/testcase/base_commit_hash` (required)
- `/src/build.sh` (improved, standalone)
- `/testcase/repo_changes.diff` (if source changes made)
- `/testcase/packages.txt` (if packages installed)

### Subtasks

1. **Identify Base Commit**: Read vulnerability description, determine suitable base commit, save to `/testcase/base_commit_hash`. If different commit needed, `git reset --hard <hash>`.

2. **Initial Build**: Run `cd <work_dir> && /src/build.sh`. Capture and analyze build errors (ignore warnings).

3. **Improve Build Script**: Make `/src/build.sh` standalone (remove undefined vars), remove fuzzer commands, add `-j$(nproc)` to make, add `-p` to mkdir, place `make clean` before configure/make, preserve existing compiler flags, check script existence before running local scripts.

4. **Fix Build Errors** (if any): For C++17 errors add `-std=c++14`, for implicit int add type declarations, for overload errors add `-D_GNU_SOURCE`. Make MINIMAL source changes. DO NOT disable sanitizers.

5. **Record Changes**: Save `git diff --no-color [BASE_COMMIT] > /testcase/repo_changes.diff`, record packages in `/testcase/packages.txt`, verify all deliverables exist.

